WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:01.990
- So we were talking about TikTok earlier,

00:00:01.990 --> 00:00:04.060
are you in love with TikTok?

00:00:04.060 --> 00:00:09.060
- I wasn't, until COVID
happened and I am now.

00:00:10.390 --> 00:00:14.620
I think, the craziness of
all things in motherhood,

00:00:14.620 --> 00:00:16.034
I did this one where--

00:00:16.034 --> 00:00:16.867
(Kelly laughing)

00:00:16.867 --> 00:00:17.700
- This is my favorite.

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:18.533
- Oh yes.

00:00:19.395 --> 00:00:23.086
- [Children] Mom!
(Kelly laughing)

00:00:23.086 --> 00:00:26.270
- So my favorite thing to
do in the whole wide world,

00:00:26.270 --> 00:00:29.700
is clean the kitchen, so
that then I can cook again.

00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:31.070
So then I can cook again,

00:00:31.070 --> 00:00:31.950
then I can clean again,

00:00:31.950 --> 00:00:33.780
then I can cook again.

00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:35.759
- Oh my gosh I feel you.

00:00:35.759 --> 00:00:37.090
(Derek laughing)
- No but literally,

00:00:37.090 --> 00:00:40.400
I think I literally was
hiding in my closet.

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:42.359
This sounds terrible, but
like I hide from my children.

00:00:42.359 --> 00:00:43.360
(Derek laughs)

00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:44.560
- [Kelly] Every parent does it,

00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:46.660
and if you say you don't you're a liar.

00:00:46.660 --> 00:00:47.920
- I hide from my children.

00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:49.195
- [Kelly] You need a minute.

00:00:49.195 --> 00:00:51.401
- And I drink wine in the closet,

00:00:51.401 --> 00:00:53.540
(Kelly laughs)
I get ready in the closet.

00:00:53.540 --> 00:00:55.577
Even today my three-year-old
Gray, he was like,

00:00:55.577 --> 00:00:57.130
"Are you going to the closet?"

00:00:57.130 --> 00:00:58.820
But literally he's like the type of child

00:00:58.820 --> 00:00:59.670
who's like, "Mom,

00:01:01.032 --> 00:01:02.187
"mom are you watching?

00:01:02.187 --> 00:01:03.020
"Mom."

00:01:03.020 --> 00:01:05.450
And I finally look over
and he (laughs) on my life,

00:01:06.390 --> 00:01:08.390
he takes a sip of water.

00:01:08.390 --> 00:01:11.470
I'm like, that's what
you wanted me to watch?

00:01:11.470 --> 00:01:14.250
- Oh my gosh it's like
Stewie from Family Guy.

00:01:14.250 --> 00:01:16.110
Mom, mommy.
- Mama.

00:01:16.110 --> 00:01:18.030
- Yeah, that's a real episode,

00:01:18.030 --> 00:01:20.110
that's not just funny.
- And so I think with TikTok,

00:01:20.110 --> 00:01:23.390
and I know Derek, I
was just like screw it,

00:01:23.390 --> 00:01:25.200
I'm just gonna show you the craziness

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:28.210
of the changing of the
diapers and the butt wiping

00:01:28.210 --> 00:01:30.528
and the bottles and the...

00:01:30.528 --> 00:01:34.030
And I have to say it's been
quite freeing in a weird way.

00:01:34.030 --> 00:01:35.640
I would always say to people,

00:01:35.640 --> 00:01:37.380
I don't really look like that,

00:01:37.380 --> 00:01:38.820
my family doesn't really look like...

00:01:38.820 --> 00:01:43.241
It's the best version of
'97 pictures taken after.

00:01:43.241 --> 00:01:44.074
(Kelly laughing)
You know what I mean?

00:01:44.074 --> 00:01:45.310
'Cause Instagram isn't real.

00:01:45.310 --> 00:01:46.143
You know what I mean?

00:01:46.143 --> 00:01:48.820
It's not, it's just the
best version of yourself,

00:01:48.820 --> 00:01:49.653
or your family

00:01:49.653 --> 00:01:50.486
or whatever it is.
- It's like the filtered

00:01:50.486 --> 00:01:52.380
version of us, yeah.
- And so I think with TikTok

00:01:52.380 --> 00:01:53.350
I think people,

00:01:53.350 --> 00:01:55.650
not that they didn't think
I did all those things,

00:01:55.650 --> 00:01:59.850
I feel I'm a good mom, but
I cook like 300 meals a day.

00:01:59.850 --> 00:02:00.683
- Oh my gosh,

00:02:00.683 --> 00:02:03.910
where would you hide in
the house if you had to?

00:02:03.910 --> 00:02:04.743
- Me?

00:02:04.743 --> 00:02:05.836
- [Kelly] yes.

00:02:05.836 --> 00:02:08.127
- It's the bathroom.

00:02:08.127 --> 00:02:09.440
You ever seen that Paul Rudd...

00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:12.370
- I literally was just
gonna say when he's playing

00:02:12.370 --> 00:02:13.203
his game on the toilet,

00:02:13.203 --> 00:02:14.240
I'm like I've totally...
- That's me.

00:02:14.240 --> 00:02:16.783
It might be TMI but that's definitely me.

00:02:16.783 --> 00:02:17.877
- No, This Is 40.

00:02:17.877 --> 00:02:19.489
That's that movie, This Is 40.

00:02:19.489 --> 00:02:21.080
- Yeah, I'm not quite there yet

00:02:21.080 --> 00:02:22.910
but that's my habit.

00:02:22.910 --> 00:02:24.050
- Dude, I'm with you.

00:02:24.050 --> 00:02:25.970
I was literally gonna
say mine is the bathroom,

00:02:25.970 --> 00:02:28.310
'cause it's the one thing
I can feel not mean about,

00:02:28.310 --> 00:02:30.160
or guilty like, mommy needs a minute.

00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:31.330
I just need to go to the bathroom

00:02:31.330 --> 00:02:33.828
and then a lot of times I'm
not going to the bathroom.

00:02:33.828 --> 00:02:35.911
(Derek laughs)
I'm just sitting in there.

00:02:35.911 --> 00:02:38.211
- If I post something on Instagram

00:02:38.211 --> 00:02:39.253
or something like that,

00:02:39.253 --> 00:02:41.576
and it could be something
I learn or read about,

00:02:41.576 --> 00:02:43.880
it's something really serious.

00:02:43.880 --> 00:02:46.800
It's all created within
the bathroom (laughs),

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:48.083
it all happens there.

00:02:48.083 --> 00:02:49.219
It's the office yeah.

00:02:49.219 --> 00:02:50.230
(Kelly and Derek laughing)

00:02:50.230 --> 00:02:52.920
- You guys, I run fake errands.

00:02:52.920 --> 00:02:56.680
I will go and pretend that
I have to go somewhere

00:02:56.680 --> 00:02:57.738
and I'll sit in my car.

00:02:57.738 --> 00:02:59.142
I did a TikTok on it.

00:02:59.142 --> 00:03:01.150
(Kelly laughing)
I literally will go

00:03:01.150 --> 00:03:02.847
and I'm like, "Bye."

00:03:02.847 --> 00:03:03.680
And they're like,

00:03:03.680 --> 00:03:05.527
"Bye, I'll miss you, I'm
going to the grocery,

00:03:05.527 --> 00:03:06.360
"I've got tons to do."

00:03:06.360 --> 00:03:07.912
I won't go anywhere ill just sit there.

00:03:07.912 --> 00:03:08.745
(Derek laughs)

00:03:08.745 --> 00:03:09.840
- [Kelly] You just need a minute,

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:10.970
and then you're a better parent.

00:03:10.970 --> 00:03:11.970
- I'm a better parent.

00:03:11.970 --> 00:03:13.780
- You're better parent
when you have some me time.

00:03:13.780 --> 00:03:15.310
- Wait, can we just discuss one thing?

00:03:15.310 --> 00:03:16.420
- Yeah.

00:03:16.420 --> 00:03:19.150
- I was backstage, were
you really in Harry Potter?

00:03:19.150 --> 00:03:19.983
- [Derek] yeah.

00:03:19.983 --> 00:03:20.816
- [Kelly] You Love Harry Potter?

00:03:20.816 --> 00:03:21.915
- Stop it.
- I guess,

00:03:21.915 --> 00:03:23.373
I'm kind of big deal.

00:03:23.373 --> 00:03:24.231
(audience laughing)

00:03:24.231 --> 00:03:25.340
- We love you.

00:03:25.340 --> 00:03:26.173
(Derek mumbles)

00:03:26.173 --> 00:03:28.500
- Since COVID, we
crushed all the episodes.

00:03:28.500 --> 00:03:30.750
I mean every Sunday, crushed it.

00:03:30.750 --> 00:03:34.310
We built, I mean it's basically an owe to

00:03:34.310 --> 00:03:35.920
Harry Potter, Lego Land, Auto House.

00:03:35.920 --> 00:03:36.753
My husband--

00:03:36.753 --> 00:03:37.740
- I love Legos.

00:03:37.740 --> 00:03:42.160
- Literally Hogwarts, 72 vodka sodas later

00:03:42.160 --> 00:03:44.040
and 61 juice boxes.

00:03:44.040 --> 00:03:46.110
He completed the castle.
- [Derek] What?

00:03:46.110 --> 00:03:47.110
- Oh there (laughs),

00:03:47.110 --> 00:03:48.160
the castle.
Look at that.

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:50.110
- You have no idea.

00:03:50.110 --> 00:03:50.943
- [Kelly] I do actually.

00:03:50.943 --> 00:03:52.919
- I want to come build that with you.

00:03:52.919 --> 00:03:54.010
That's so fun.

00:03:54.010 --> 00:03:57.260
- My house, my whole breakfast
area, and the kids play,

00:03:57.260 --> 00:03:58.350
I have a whole like kids arts,

00:03:58.350 --> 00:04:01.990
it looks like a little school
section, Legos are everywhere.

00:04:01.990 --> 00:04:03.900
- You love Legos.
- It's so therapeutic.

00:04:03.900 --> 00:04:05.070
You should join in.

00:04:05.070 --> 00:04:05.910
- I do.

00:04:05.910 --> 00:04:06.970
I'm not as fast.

00:04:06.970 --> 00:04:08.520
He'll do like, "You're
not as fast as daddy."

00:04:08.520 --> 00:04:10.735
- Oh see, I'm like that with my kids.

00:04:10.735 --> 00:04:12.450
(laughs)I'm so bad.

00:04:12.450 --> 00:04:13.857
I'm like, "Oh, did you
want mommy to do it?

00:04:13.857 --> 00:04:14.970
"Oh, I'm fine doing it."

00:04:14.970 --> 00:04:16.390
and then cut to it, they're coloring

00:04:16.390 --> 00:04:19.240
and I'm like putting together
this thing on my own.

00:04:19.240 --> 00:04:20.470
(laughing)
- I swear that is my husband.

00:04:20.470 --> 00:04:22.600
He will be--
- [Kelly] It's so good.

00:04:22.600 --> 00:04:24.380
- He might have something
to drink next to him,

00:04:24.380 --> 00:04:26.530
